course: dictionary
lesson: 13653
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning to use. «Her knee was inflamed after she bumped it on the step.» Red, hot and sore are clues about the body, so inflamed means red, swollen and sore.
explain: The same word can also describe feelings. «The rude speech inflamed the crowd, and people began to shout.» Shouting is a clue that people became much angrier, so inflamed means made more angry here.
explain: To check your meaning, put it into the sentence in place of the hard word. «Her knee was red, swollen and sore» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Inflamed means red, swollen, hot and sore, usually because of an injury or infection.
fact: Inflamed can also mean made much angrier or more excited, as in «an inflamed crowd».
fact: Inflame is a verb, and inflamed is its past form: «His words inflamed the argument» means his words made the argument worse.
fact: Doctors talk about an inflamed throat, inflamed tonsils or inflamed skin.
fact: Inflammation is the body's way of healing: redness, heat, swelling and pain help an injury get better.
exercise: «Her knee was inflamed after she bumped it on the step.» What does inflamed mean here? | Made happy | *Red, swollen, hot and sore | Cool and calm | Covered in mud
exercise: «The rude speech inflamed the crowd, and people began to shout.» What does inflamed mean here? | Cleaned and tidied | Sleepy and quiet | Bored and tired | *Made much angrier
exercise: «His cruel words inflamed the argument.» What does inflamed mean here? | Wrapped in paper | Cooled down slowly | *Made the bad situation worse | Helped everyone agree
test: «The nurse said the cut looked inflamed and warm.» What does inflamed mean here? | Clean and dry | Very long and thin | Frozen solid | *Red, swollen and sore
test: «The king's speech inflamed the people, who marched angrily through the streets.» What does inflamed mean here? | Put out, like a fire | *Made much angrier | Calmed and peaceful | Bright and shiny
exam: Which meaning of inflamed fits «The skin around the bite was inflamed»? | *Red, hot and sore, because of the body's response to a bite | Covered in paper and tape | Made happier and calmer | Red, hot and sore
